# ---------------- TK4_MuzzleFlash.events (Task 16 Part C.5) ----------------
# One flash per shot: `TK_Player.events` does `spawn MuzzleFlash at me offset 30`, so this block
# runs on a fresh clone each time — never on the scene's template.
#
# The `my spawnedFrom` gate is what keeps the template usable: an EventSheet component is
# attached even on an inactive actor, so without the gate the template would run this block at
# scene start, flash once at its own position and `destroy me` itself — leaving nothing for the
# first real shot to clone (which is why the flash "went missing"). A clone carries
# `my spawnedFrom` = the template's name; the template itself does not.

when me appears
  my spawnedFrom is "MuzzleFlash"
  print "TK4 muzzle: clone appeared"
  play particle "muzzle"
  print "TK4 muzzle: particle played"
  enable light
  set light intensity to 3
  set light color to "1 0.8 0.2"
  wait 0.1 seconds
  disable light
  stop particle "muzzle"
  print "TK4 muzzle: flash done"
  destroy me
